56" "7e5d1f1c51d7a1de2d529f4b6ef38cefe32e6d536e5cb78261131e6234cc5abb"} {"question" "q-8858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+y=0 \\\\ 3x-6y=2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063974/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e5d1f1c51d7a1de2d529f4b6ef38cefe32e6d536e5cb78261131e6234cc5abb"} {"question" "q-8858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-6)-1\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063974/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e5d1f1c51d7a1de2d529f4b6ef38cefe32e6d536e5cb78261131e6234cc5abb"} {"question" "q-8858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063974/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "924c7aa0a2799399d689ea46bce23b695fb145fe4235247d2d1a84c5d90c53a4"} {"question" "q-8858" "field" "selec